The root cause is in `pandas/io/formats/xml.py`, in `_BaseXMLFormatter._build_attribs` and `_build_elems`. Both call plain `str(...)` on the cell value, which turns Python bools into `"True"`/`"False"` instead of the `xs:boolean` literals `"true"`/`"false"`.

A minimal fix is to special-case bools before falling back to `str()`:

```python
@final
def _get_xml_value(self, val: Any) -> str:
    if isinstance(val, bool):
        return "true" if val else "false"
    return str(val)
```
